{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_001's core claim — that SRC_006 and SRC_008 'each verdict references the other's independence as justification' — is an unverifiable factual assertion about those targets' contents. The target summary provides no quoted evidence from SRC_006 or SRC_008 demonstrating this mutual cross-referencing; the circular-dependency diagnosis is constructed from a paraphrase, not from exhibited text. Under §11.3 the ritual requires sustained flags to rest on demonstrable evidence, not on a critic's characterization of unseen verdicts. The argument further assumes that the ritual lacks any mechanism to detect circular corroboration, but no evidence shows the adjudication framework's design; the conclusion that the loop 'cannot' be distinguished from genuine corroboration is therefore unsupported speculation rather than an auditable finding.","premise":"An adjudication-ritual audit flag must be sustained on evidence that is exhibited or quoted, not on a critic's uncorroborated description of artifacts not shown in the target.","target":"003bad6be1915b81a9c4a52f30a9e8ecce4ed196f68c76cabe6c2c10cccde740"}]}